​
{
"cells": [
  {​
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "header",
   "metadata": {},​
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f2027, #203a43, #2c5364); padding:20px; border-radius:15px; color:white; text-align:center\">\n",
    "    <h1>🛰️ Atelier GDAL expert – Image satellite MTG plein disque</h1>\n",
    "    <p>Manipulations 100% Bash | Reprojection | Découpage | Gamma | Côtes | Texte | Couleurs</p>\n",
    "    <p><code>/toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif</code> → dossier <code>RESULTS/</code></p>\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "setup",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#e6f7ff; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #1890ff; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>📁 Préparation : création du dossier RESULTS et définition des variables</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "On crée le dossier de sortie et on fixe des variables d’environnement pour éviter de répéter les chemins."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_prep",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!mkdir -p RESULTS\n",
    "!export IMG=/toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif\n",
    "!export OUT=RESULTS"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "gdalinfo",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#fff7e6; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #faad14; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>🔍 1. Information sur l’image source (gdalinfo)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`gdalinfo -stats` affiche la projection, l’étendue, le nombre de bandes, les statistiques. Options utiles : `-mm`, `-hist`, `-json`.\n",
    "\n",
    "🗜️ **Miniature** : on utilise `convert` d’ImageMagick pour redimensionner à 400 pixels de large."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_info",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!gdalinfo -stats /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif\n",
    "!convert /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/orig_thumb.jpg\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image; display(Image(filename='RESULTS/orig_thumb.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "reproject",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#e6fffa; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #13c2c2; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>🔄 2. Reprojection dans 5 systèmes (gdalwarp)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`gdalwarp` change la projection. Options : `-t_srs` (cible), `-r lanczos` (rééchantillonnage de qualité), `-co COMPRESS=LZW` (compression).\n",
    "\n",
    "On produit : WGS84, Mercator, Stéréographique, Orthographique, GEOS (native)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_reproj",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs EPSG:4326 -r lanczos -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/reproj_WGS84.tif\n",
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs EPSG:3857 -r lanczos -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/reproj_Mercator.tif\n",
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs \"+proj=stere +lat_0=90 +lon_0=0 +k=0.994 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +datum=WGS84 +units=m\" -r lanczos -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/reproj_StereoNorth.tif\n",
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs \"+proj=ortho +lat_0=50 +lon_0=10 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +datum=WGS84\" -r lanczos -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/reproj_OrthoEurope.tif\n",
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs \"+proj=geos +lon_0=0 +h=35785831 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +ellps=WGS84 +units=m\" -r near -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/reproj_GEOS_native.tif\n",
    "\n",
    "# Miniatures\n",
    "!convert RESULTS/reproj_WGS84.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/thumb_WGS84.jpg\n",
    "display(Image(filename='RESULTS/thumb_WGS84.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cut",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#f9f0ff; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #722ed1; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>✂️ 3. Découpage sur la France (avec shapefile ou bbox)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`gdalwarp -cutline` + `-crop_to_cutline` : découpage exact sur un polygone. Si le shapefile est absent, on utilise `-te` (bbox)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_cut",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Avec shapefile France (si disponible)\n",
    "#!gdalwarp -cutline data/france.shp -crop_to_cutline -cblend 5 -dstalpha -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/france_cutline.tif\n",
    "\n",
    "# Variante : découpage par bbox en WGS84 (France métropolitaine)\n",
    "!gdalwarp -t_srs EPSG:4326 -te -5 41 10 51 -crop_to_cutline -co COMPRESS=LZW /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/france_bbox.tif\n",
    "!convert RESULTS/france_bbox.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/thumb_france.jpg\n",
    "display(Image(filename='RESULTS/thumb_france.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "gamma",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#fff1f0; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #f5222d; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>⚡ 4. Correction gamma exponentielle (gdal_calc.py)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`gdal_calc.py -A image --A_band=1 --calc=\"255*(A/255.0)**(1/0.5)\"` applique gamma = 0.5 (exposant 2). On répète pour les 3 bandes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_gamma",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!gdal_calc.py -A /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif --A_band=1 -B /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif --B_band=2 -C /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif --C_band=3 \\\n",
    "    --outfile=RESULTS/gamma_correction.tif \\\n",
    "    --calc=\"255*(A/255.0)**2\" --calc=\"255*(B/255.0)**2\" --calc=\"255*(C/255.0)**2\" \\\n",
    "    --type=Byte --co=COMPRESS=LZW\n",
    "!convert RESULTS/gamma_correction.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/thumb_gamma.jpg\n",
    "display(Image(filename='RESULTS/thumb_gamma.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "coastline",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#e6f7ff; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #1890ff; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>🌊 5. Ajout d’un trait de côte (shapefile → raster)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "On combine `gdal_rasterize` (pour brûler les lignes) et `gdal_calc.py` pour fusionner."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_coast",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Si un shapefile de côtes existe (ex. ne_110m_coastline.shp)\n",
    "#!gdal_rasterize -b 1 -b 2 -b 3 -burn 255 -burn 255 -burn 255 -l ne_110m_coastline data/ne_110m_coastline.shp RESULTS/coast_mask.tif\n",
    "#!gdal_calc.py -A RESULTS/reproj_WGS84.tif -B RESULTS/coast_mask.tif --outfile=RESULTS/with_coast.tif --calc=\"numpy.where(B==255,255,A)\" --type=Byte\n",
    "#!convert RESULTS/with_coast.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/thumb_coast.jpg\n",
    "#display(Image(filename='RESULTS/thumb_coast.jpg'))\n",
    "\n",
    "echo \"⚠️ Exemple – remplacer par vos chemins réels de shapefile côtes.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "text",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#f6ffed; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #52c41a; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>✍️ 6. Ajout de texte avec ImageMagick</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`convert` permet d’ajouter des annotations (`-annotate`) avec police, taille, couleur, position."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_text",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!convert RESULTS/reproj_WGS84.tif \\\n",
    "    -font Arial -pointsize 20 -fill white -gravity NorthWest -annotate +15+15 \"MTG-1 2024-04-27\" \\\n",
    "    -font Arial -pointsize 16 -fill yellow -gravity SouthEast -annotate +15+15 \"GDAL processing\" \\\n",
    "    RESULTS/annotated.jpg\n",
    "display(Image(filename='RESULTS/annotated.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "extract",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#fff0f5; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #eb2f96; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>📍 7. Extraction de valeur à une coordonnée (gdallocationinfo)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "`gdallocationinfo -wgs84 image.tif lon lat` donne les valeurs des bandes au point (46.5°N, 1.5°E)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_extract",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!gdallocationinfo -wgs84 /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif 1.5 46.5\n",
    "!gdallocationinfo -valonly -wgs84 /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif 1.5 46.5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "colormap",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#f4f0ec; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #8c8c8c; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>🎨 8. Appliquer une palette à un raster monobande (gdaldem color-relief)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "On extrait une bande (niveaux de gris), on crée une table de couleurs (fichier texte), puis `gdaldem color-relief`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bash_colormap",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extraire la bande 1\n",
    "!gdal_translate -b 1 /toto/tata/titi/mon_image.tif RESULTS/gray_band.tif\n",
    "# Créer une palette (ex. du bleu au rouge)\n",
    "!echo \"0 0 0 255\n",
    "64 0 128 255\n",
    "128 255 255 0\n",
    "192 255 0 0\n",
    "255 255 255 255\" > RESULTS/palette.txt\n",
    "# Appliquer\n",
    "!gdaldem color-relief -co COMPRESS=LZW RESULTS/gray_band.tif RESULTS/palette.txt RESULTS/colored.tif\n",
    "!convert RESULTS/colored.tif -resize 400x RESULTS/thumb_colormap.jpg\n",
    "display(Image(filename='RESULTS/thumb_colormap.jpg'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "extra",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"background-color:#ebf5ff; padding:10px; border-left:5px solid #1677ff; margin:20px 0\">\n",
    "    <b>✨ 9. Idées supplémentaires (commandes bash GDAL)</b>\n",
    "</div>\n",
    "\n",
    "*   **Redimensionnement simple** : `convert image.tif -resize 190x1080 image_redim.jpg`\n",
    "*   **NDVI** (si bandes disponibles) : `gdal_calc.py -A red.tif -B nir.tif --outfile=ndvi.tif --calc=\"((B-A)/(B+A+0.001))*100\"`\n",
    "*   **Mosaïquage** : `gdalbuildvrt mosaic.vrt *.tif` puis `gdal_translate mosaic.vrt mosaic.tif`\n",
    "*   **Pyramides (overviews)** : `gdaladdo -r average image.tif 2 4 8 16`\n",
    "*   **Cloud optimized GeoTIFF** : `gdal_translate image.tif cog.tif -of COG -co COMPRESS=LZW`\n",
    "\n",
    "🎉 **Félicitations !** Vous avez manipulé une image satellite avec les commandes GDAL pures, généré des miniatures, et tout cela en Bash dans Jupyter."
   ]
  }
],
